  Qt for Python (PySide6)   https://www.qt.io/qt-for-python
  Qt 6                      https://www.qt.io/

PDFSafe's graphical interface links against Qt via PySide6, which is licensed
under the LGPL v3. PDFSafe itself is Apache-2.0; the two are compatible because
Qt is *dynamically* linked.

To honour the LGPL, PDFSafe is distributed as a directory bundle (not a single
packed executable) in which the Qt libraries are separate, replaceable `.dll`
files under `_internal/PySide6/`. You may replace those libraries with your own
build of Qt of the same major version and the application will use them.

The corresponding source for Qt and PySide6 is available from the URLs above.
If you cannot obtain it there, open an issue and we will provide it.

Note: the command-line interface (`pdfsafe`) does not link Qt at all and is
Apache-2.0 throughout.
